  {
   "id": 530780,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<iframe src=\"https://www.openstax.org/l/28torque\"></iframe>\n<p>If the net torque acting on the ruler from the example was positive instead of zero, what would this say about the angular acceleration? What would happen to the ruler over time?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1038450,
     "content_html": "The ruler is in a state of rotational equilibrium so it will not rotate about its center of mass. Thus, the angular acceleration will be zero."
    },
    {
     "id": 1038451,
     "content_html": "The ruler is not in a state of rotational equilibrium so it will not rotate about its center of mass. Thus, the angular acceleration will be zero."
    },
    {
     "id": 1038452,
     "content_html": "The ruler is not in a state of rotational equilibrium so it will rotate about its center of mass. Thus, the angular acceleration will be non-zero."
    },
    {
     "id": 1038453,
     "content_html": "The ruler is in a state of rotational equilibrium so it will rotate about its center of mass. Thus, the angular acceleration will be non-zero."
    }
   ],
